## §6 — Maintain

| Area | What you do |
|------|-------------|
| **Patches** | `apt upgrade` (Debian) or `dnf update redis` (RHEL) in staging first. Check release notes for breaking config changes. |
| **Config** | `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (or `/etc/redis.conf`) in **Git**. Validate with `redis-server --test-memory 256` and restart. |
| **Memory** | Monitor `INFO memory` — `used_memory` vs `maxmemory`. Alert at **80%**. |
| **Persistence** | Check `INFO persistence` — `rdb_last_bgsave_status`, `aof_last_bgrewrite_status`. Alert on failures. |
| **Replication** | `INFO replication` — `connected_slaves`, `master_link_status`. Replica lag = `master_repl_offset - slave_repl_offset`. |
| **Slow log** | `SLOWLOG GET 10` — commands exceeding `slowlog-log-slower-than` (default 10ms). |
| **Backups** | Copy `dump.rdb` off-host periodically. For AOF, run `BGREWRITEAOF` to compact, then backup. |
| **Security** | `requirepass`, `rename-command KEYS ""`, TLS (Redis 6+), firewall (§3 firewall section). |
| **Sentinel** | `redis-cli -p 26379 SENTINEL masters` — check quorum, failover count, last-ok-ping-reply. |

**Change window:** announce → baseline `INFO` snapshot → one parameter change → `redis-cli CONFIG SET` for live changes or restart for file-only params → verify `INFO` + test app → rollback plan is previous config file in Git.

