## §10 — Useful sysctl and OS tuning (Linux)

```bash
# Overcommit for RDB fork
echo 'vm.overcommit_memory=1' | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/99-redis.conf

# Disable THP (transparent huge pages) — Redis warns on startup
echo never | sudo tee /sys/kernel/mm/transparent_hugepage/enabled

# somaxconn for high connection counts
echo 'net.core.somaxconn=65535' | sudo tee -a /etc/sysctl.d/99-redis.conf

sudo sysctl --system
```

Check Redis startup logs (`journalctl -u redis`) — it warns about each of these if misconfigured.

